# Wraps qwen3.8 (27.3B, capabilities: completion/vision/tools/thinking, native
# 262,144-token context) for ScryingPool's judge_model + verify_model role: /scry
# routing, expansion, candidate judging and per-finalist art verification, plus
# /oracle routing, expansion and judging. See config.toml for why both keys point
# at the same model name.
#
# Build:
#   ollama create scryingpool-qwen3.8 -f models/scryingpool.Modelfile
#
# Rebuild after editing this file with the same command — `ollama create` is
# idempotent and overwrites the existing tag.

FROM qwen3.8

# --- num_ctx ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Not decoration. When num_ctx is unset, Ollama does not pick some sane
# fallback — it sizes the KV cache for the MODEL'S OWN advertised context
# window, 262,144 tokens here. That is exactly the bug already documented at
# cts/oracle_judge.py::JUDGE_NUM_CTX: one real 2,153-token judge prompt got a
# context allocated for 262,144 tokens and blew a 300s timeout.
#
# Some call sites already pin their own num_ctx per request and are
# unaffected by this default either way: JUDGE_NUM_CTX=8192 and
# ROUTER_NUM_CTX=4096 / EXPANSION_NUM_CTX=2048 in cts/oracle_judge.py and
# cts/oracle_search.py. But cts/judge.py's judge_batch() and
# verify_finalists(), and cts/search.py's route() and expand(), never set
# num_ctx in their request options — for those calls (the /scry pipeline this
# model now serves), this Modelfile default is the ONLY thing bounding
# context, not a backstop.
#
# Sized from the real worst case, not a guess: cts/judge.py batches up to
# BATCH_SIZE=10 candidates per judge call, each showing up to
# MAX_PROPS_SHOWN=40 propositions plus both description layers. Building that
# prompt from the actual shipped corpus (data/commanders.db) using the 10
# longest-description artworks in the whole 5,530-artwork set — the real
# worst case any batch could ever draw — produced a 63,085-character prompt:
# roughly 15.8k-18k tokens depending on chars-per-token assumed for this
# tokenizer, plus a ~1-2k token structured-JSON response for 10 judgments.
# 32768 gives that ~40-70% headroom while still being an eighth of the
# model's native window, so the VRAM/latency win over leaving it unset is
# still enormous. Every other call path here — oracle judge (8192), oracle
# router (4096), oracle expand (2048), /scry route()/expand() — fits inside
# it with room to spare.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# --- temperature --------------------------------------------------------
# 0 for deterministic judging. Every call site in this repo already passes
# its own explicit "temperature" in the request options (0 for judging,
# routing and verification; 0.3 for the two theme-expansion calls), so in
# practice this value is never exercised by ScryingPool code today — it
# exists as a safe default for any caller (a manual curl, a future code
# path) that forgets to set one, rather than inheriting qwen3.8's own
# default of 1.
PARAMETER temperature 0
